From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 03:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] stigenable: drop three packages the hardening does not need

Each added package is attack surface on a system whose purpose is to be
hardened, so KS_STIG_PACKAGES should name only what the role actually uses.
Three entries do not:

libselinux-utils - the role never invokes any of its binaries (getenforce,
setenforce, sestatus, restorecon, fixfiles); a grep over every *.yml in
stig-hardening finds no reference. It is also already a Requires of
selinux-policy, so it is installed either way and listing it changes nothing.
The relabel service calls /usr/sbin/restorecon, which comes from
policycoreutils, not from this package.

ntp - installed and then never configured. handlers/main.yml defines
"restart ntpd", "restart chrony" and "restart timesyncd", but no task
notifies any of them, and outside handlers/main.yml the string "ntp" does not
occur anywhere in the role: no ntp.conf/chrony.conf/timesyncd.conf task, no
server or pool setting, and no PHTN control for time synchronisation among
the 117 in the role. (README.md documents a var_ntp_servers extra-var that
nothing consumes.) Photon 5.0 also has no package named ntp; it resolves to
ntpsec via Provides. Removing it leaves a daemon uninstalled rather than
installed-and-ignored.

libgcrypt - present only to work around a packaging bug, as the role itself
records at tasks/photon.yml: "Currently a bug in the aide package that does
not upgrade libgcrypt to the needed version". The fix belongs in aide.spec,
which now carries a versioned Requires, so the workaround is unnecessary.

Time synchronisation being unimplemented is a separate finding and is not
addressed here; this change only stops installing a package for it.

Co-Authored-By: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
 photon_installer/stigenable.py | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/photon_installer/stigenable.py b/photon_installer/stigenable.py
--- a/photon_installer/stigenable.py
+++ b/photon_installer/stigenable.py
@@ -23,10 +23,7 @@
     "rsyslog",
     "openssl-fips-provider",
     "selinux-policy",
-    "libselinux-utils",
-    "ntp",
-    "aide",
-    "libgcrypt"
+    "aide"
 ]
 
 
